<div class="card page-wide pay-guide">
  <h1>Supplier &amp; logistics partner payments — step by step</h1>
  <p class="muted">What to type in each box when a supplier or a logistics partner (CHA, transport, freight forwarder) asks to be paid. Every screenshot below is the real order page; the order, the supplier and the partners are samples.</p>

  <div class="pay-guide-rules">
    <p><strong>Two rules cover almost everything:</strong></p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Bill first, then pay.</strong> Add the bill they sent you (with the scan attached), then record the payment against that bill.</li>
      <li><strong>Proforma or tax invoice?</strong> A <em>proforma</em> (advance request) asks for money now — it is <em>not</em> a cost. A <em>tax invoice</em> (final bill) is the real bill — it <em>is</em> the order's cost. When the tax invoice arrives, pick the proforma it replaces, so what you already paid counts towards it.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <p class="pay-guide-download"><strong>Full guide to print or share:</strong> the <em>Supplier &amp; Logistics Payments Guide</em> (21 pages, PDF and Word, with every step marked on the screenshots and a one-page cheat sheet) is in the <a href="/reference-docs">Reference Library</a>.</p>

